{% comment %}
  sections/testimonials.liquid

  Customer quotes, as a grid or a carousel.

  ## What changed in Phase 3

  Same duplication as the other two: a carousel branch carrying the arrows, the
  pause button and the live region, and a grid branch carrying none of them.

  The pause button matters here more than anywhere else in the theme. Autoplay
  is genuinely useful for testimonials and merchants switch it on, and moving
  content that cannot be stopped is a WCAG 2.2.2 failure. In the old markup the
  control existed only in one branch; the shell renders it whenever autoplay is
  available, so it cannot go missing by choosing the other layout.
{% endcomment %}

<div
  class="testimonials color-scheme-container color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}"
  {% render 'spacing', section: section.settings %}
> 
  <div class="{% render 'container', width: section.settings.container_width %}">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <div class="testimonials__header testimonials__header--{{ section.settings.alignment }}">
        <h2 class="testimonials__heading">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</h2>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
      The carousel element, written here rather than through
      `snippets/carousel-shell.liquid`.

      Its slides are theme blocks, and `{% content_for %}` cannot have its output
      captured - theme-check reports it as an error, because Shopify renders
      blocks with their editor bindings attached and buffering that output into a
      variable is not something the platform supports. Handing slides to the shell
      snippet meant capturing them first.

      The shell is not duplicated. `carousel-shell-attrs` writes the element's
      attributes and `carousel-shell-tail` writes the arrows, pagination, pause
      button and live region - the same markup `carousel-shell.liquid` emits, from
      the same sub-snippets. Only the element and its track live here, which is
      the minimum that lets `content_for` sit inside the track.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign cs_layout = section.settings.layout
      assign cs_layout_mobile = section.settings.layout_mobile
      assign cs_label = 'sections.testimonials.carousel_label' | t

      assign cs_is_carousel = false
      if cs_layout == 'carousel' or cs_layout_mobile == 'carousel'
        assign cs_is_carousel = true
      endif
    -%}

    <swiper-carousel
      {% render 'carousel-shell-attrs',
         settings: section.settings,
         layout: cs_layout,
         layout_mobile: cs_layout_mobile,
         classes: 'testimonials__carousel',
         columns_desktop: section.settings.columns_desktop,
         columns_tablet: section.settings.columns_tablet,
         columns_mobile: section.settings.columns_mobile %}
    >
      <div
        class="carousel-shell__track testimonials__grid"
        data-ref="track"
        {% if cs_is_carousel %}aria-label="{{ cs_label | escape }}"{% endif %}
      >
        {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      </div>

      {% render 'carousel-shell-tail',
         settings: section.settings,
         layout: cs_layout,
         layout_mobile: cs_layout_mobile %}
    </swiper-carousel>

  </div>
</div>


